- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/channelextract.html
- Summary (EN): Pulls one channel out of a layer, VDB or attribute and outputs it as a single Mono result named channel. It is a simpler alternative to Channel Split with one output.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud channelextract extrait un seul canal d'une couche multicanale et le sort sous forme de couche Mono.

- Inputs meaning: ["channels: multichannel layer, VDB or attribute to extract from"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Signature", "meaning": "Layer type the input accepts; see the Signatures section of the glossary"}, {"name": "Channel to Extract", "meaning": "Channel index; default 0 is Red (x), 1 is green"}]

- Caveats: ["If the requested channel is missing, the standard channel extension rules apply; the page does not describe them"]

